  "content": {
    "id": "p21-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Let $p$ and $q$ be the roots of the quadratic $x^2+7x+5$. Find a quadratic with integer coefficients whose roots are:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p21-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac1p$ and $\\dfrac1q$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5x^2+7x+1$",
          "worked": "Vieta’s formulas give $p+q=-7$ and $pq=5$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1p+\\frac1q&=\\frac{p+q}{pq}\\\\\\frac1p+\\frac1q&=-\\frac75\\\\\\frac1p\\cdot\\frac1q&=\\frac15\\end{align*}$$\nThe monic quadratic is $x^2+\\frac75x+\\frac15$. Multiplying by $5$ gives $5x^2+7x+1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$2p$ and $2q$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^2+14x+20$",
          "worked": "Vieta’s formulas give $p+q=-7$ and $pq=5$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2p+2q&=2(-7)\\\\2p+2q&=-14\\\\(2p)(2q)&=4(5)\\\\(2p)(2q)&=20\\end{align*}$$\nThe quadratic is $x^2+14x+20$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$p^2$ and $q^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^2-39x+25$",
          "worked": "Vieta’s formulas give $p+q=-7$ and $pq=5$.\n$$\\begin{align*}p^2+q^2&=(p+q)^2-2pq\\\\p^2+q^2&=(-7)^2-2(5)\\\\p^2+q^2&=39\\\\p^2q^2&=(pq)^2\\\\p^2q^2&=25\\end{align*}$$\nThe quadratic is $x^2-39x+25$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac pq$ and $\\dfrac qp$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5x^2-39x+5$",
          "worked": "Vieta’s formulas give $p+q=-7$ and $pq=5$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac pq+\\frac qp&=\\frac{p^2+q^2}{pq}\\\\\\frac pq+\\frac qp&=\\frac{(p+q)^2-2pq}{pq}\\\\\\frac pq+\\frac qp&=\\frac{49-10}{5}\\\\\\frac pq+\\frac qp&=\\frac{39}{5}\\\\\\frac pq\\cdot\\frac qp&=1\\end{align*}$$\nThe monic quadratic is $x^2-\\frac{39}{5}x+1$. Multiplying by $5$ gives $5x^2-39x+5$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 82
      }
    ]
  },
